WEBVTT

00:01:32.610 --> 00:01:42.950
I never thought

00:01:34.070 --> 00:01:42.950
that I would encounter an XX-jellyfish (sic)

00:01:38.360 --> 00:01:42.950
in this place

00:02:08.540 --> 00:02:12.110
<i>I just happened to come 
to this beach to swim.</i>

00:02:12.650 --> 00:02:15.980
<i>and was stung on the left 
arm by a jellyfish.</i>

00:02:16.980 --> 00:02:20.760
<i>I need to find a doctor as soon as possible.</i>

00:02:21.730 --> 00:02:24.050
<i>My precious blood.</i>

00:02:24.950 --> 00:02:32.020
<i>The blood I should be feeding 
Mai is flowing out of me...</i>

00:02:33.420 --> 00:02:42.890
Capital Under Martial Law

00:03:00.740 --> 00:03:02.880
Excuse me for asking, but...

00:03:02.880 --> 00:03:04.740
Ask us anything.

00:03:04.740 --> 00:03:06.630
After all, we're public servants.

00:03:06.630 --> 00:03:11.940
We're obligated to answer 
the taxpayers' questions.

00:03:11.940 --> 00:03:15.370
By the way, this armored fighting 
vehicle you're looking at...

00:03:15.370 --> 00:03:19.220
...is the Type 16 mobile combat 
vehicle used by the Mobile Division,

00:03:19.220 --> 00:03:24.120
also known as the Mobile Brigade 
of the Rapid Deployment Regiment,

00:03:24.120 --> 00:03:26.740
as well as by the Reconnaissance Combat 
Battalions of Local Deployment Divisions.

00:03:26.740 --> 00:03:28.450
Actually—

00:03:28.450 --> 00:03:34.360
Developed in 2007 to replace 
tanks on some missions and reduce

00:03:34.360 --> 00:03:37.830
the number of tanks in service, as 
well as improve redeployment speed,

00:03:37.830 --> 00:03:41.130
it officially entered service in 2016.

00:03:41.130 --> 00:03:44.420
Utilizing an independent suspension 
system with four wheels

00:03:44.420 --> 00:03:46.900
on each side for a total of eight wheels,

00:03:46.900 --> 00:03:49.910
it comes equipped with a 
Japanese-made 105 mm L/52 gun

00:03:49.910 --> 00:03:55.660
and 7.62 mm machine gun on 
a fully rotating turret.

00:03:55.660 --> 00:04:00.340
Its firepower is equal to or even 
greater than the Type 74's.

00:04:00.690 --> 00:04:02.630
That's not what I—

00:04:02.630 --> 00:04:07.780
The Type 16 mobile combat vehicle 
overcomes the low accuracy and recoil

00:04:07.780 --> 00:04:12.770
of conventional wheeled tanks with 
its advanced fire-control system

00:04:12.770 --> 00:04:15.590
and vibration control technology.

00:04:15.590 --> 00:04:20.230
Its accuracy is high even 
when firing on the move.

00:04:20.230 --> 00:04:22.070
I'm not asking about that.

00:04:22.070 --> 00:04:24.590
Is there a doctor around here?

00:04:24.990 --> 00:04:25.950
I see.

00:04:25.950 --> 00:04:27.990
In other words, you mean...

00:04:27.990 --> 00:04:30.080
You're looking for a doctor.

00:04:30.080 --> 00:04:37.590
If you guys have any love at all 
for Mai, then take me to a doctor.

00:04:38.210 --> 00:04:39.320
I see.

00:04:39.320 --> 00:04:42.750
I'm finally beginning to understand 
what you're trying to say.

00:04:42.750 --> 00:04:46.180
In other words, this is 
what you're asking us.

00:04:47.720 --> 00:04:51.560
<b>Where can I find a doctor?!</b>

00:04:51.960 --> 00:04:54.520
Enough with the mean-spirited jokes!

00:04:54.520 --> 00:04:58.590
You'd point your guns against 
your own blood sister?

00:04:58.590 --> 00:05:01.990
I could die here!

00:05:04.350 --> 00:05:09.350
My precious blood is flowing out of my body.

00:05:09.660 --> 00:05:11.810
Someone. Anyone.

00:05:11.810 --> 00:05:13.400
Somebody tell me!

00:05:13.410 --> 00:05:17.370
<b>Where can I find a doctor?!</b>

00:05:17.640 --> 00:05:21.860
I know. If I go to a school, 
there might be a doctor there.

00:05:22.840 --> 00:05:24.180
That's it.

00:05:34.290 --> 00:05:39.380
Anyway, these railroad tracks 
sure are difficult to walk on.

00:05:40.320 --> 00:05:45.260
I'm beginning to feel impatient.

00:05:46.880 --> 00:05:51.190
The flies. The flies...

00:05:52.300 --> 00:05:57.310
The flies rub their hands and feet.

00:05:58.060 --> 00:06:03.550
Strike not the fly that rubs its hands

00:06:06.150 --> 00:06:09.150
and feet together.

00:06:28.840 --> 00:06:31.620
This train arrived at just the right time,

00:06:32.010 --> 00:06:38.010
but isn't it heading back towards 
the direction I came from?

00:06:38.410 --> 00:06:41.070
Try sitting on the other side.

00:06:41.070 --> 00:06:45.680
Then you'll feel like you're traveling 
in the opposite direction.

00:06:46.250 --> 00:06:49.160
Now that you mention it, you're right.

00:06:49.160 --> 00:06:52.700
You don't even have to go to school 
to learn about that principle.

00:06:52.700 --> 00:06:54.820
Everybody knows that.

00:06:54.820 --> 00:06:56.280
That's right.

00:06:56.820 --> 00:06:59.820
I need to remain pragmatic.

00:06:59.820 --> 00:07:02.950
Despite being an otaku, you saved my life.

00:07:02.950 --> 00:07:05.600
What do you mean, "despite?"

00:07:16.210 --> 00:07:19.440
This is the street corner where I started.

00:07:23.580 --> 00:07:43.060
Capital Under Martial Law

00:07:25.750 --> 00:07:29.400
I've wasted so much time.

00:07:30.830 --> 00:07:36.200
All right. In that case, 
I'll thoroughly search the entire town.

00:07:36.900 --> 00:07:38.710
No, in this case,

00:07:38.710 --> 00:07:42.340
it's more grammatically correct to say I'll 
"through-lilly" search the entire town.

00:07:51.260 --> 00:07:54.870
Damn it! This neighborhood 
is nothing but urologists!

00:07:54.870 --> 00:07:58.200
I'm not an old man with 
an enlarged prostate!

00:08:00.180 --> 00:08:07.380
Anyway, this place is as 
quiet as a ghost town.

00:08:10.920 --> 00:08:33.820
<b>Blended Bath</b>

00:08:12.130 --> 00:08:13.270
What's this?

00:08:13.920 --> 00:08:16.920
That's a sign for a public bath.

00:08:17.790 --> 00:08:20.310
That's odd, though.

00:08:21.200 --> 00:08:25.530
I feel like I've always known 
about this public bath.

00:08:25.950 --> 00:08:29.170
It feels so familiar.

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:31.820
That candy shop, too.

00:08:33.820 --> 00:09:30.790
<b>Hallelujah</b>

00:08:33.820 --> 00:09:30.790
Tobacco

00:08:40.060 --> 00:08:42.470
How nostalgic.

00:08:42.470 --> 00:08:44.580
They're playing a game of menko.

00:08:44.930 --> 00:08:48.860
But my generation shouldn't 
know about that game.

00:08:50.180 --> 00:08:51.500
You kids.

00:08:51.500 --> 00:08:54.680
You seem to be playing Proletariat Detectives

00:08:54.680 --> 00:08:57.560
versus Petite Bourgeoisie with Twenty Faces menko.

00:08:57.560 --> 00:08:58.930
So, what?

00:08:58.930 --> 00:09:00.610
You can't have our menko cards.

00:09:00.610 --> 00:09:02.980
If you want some, 
you'll have to buy them yourself.

00:09:02.980 --> 00:09:06.560
Perhaps I'll purchase that mask, then.

00:09:06.560 --> 00:09:08.400
Anyway, you...

00:09:08.400 --> 00:09:11.350
...look just like the old lady 
attendant at the blended bath.

00:09:11.350 --> 00:09:13.320
You're practically identical.

00:09:13.320 --> 00:09:15.630
Do we look that similar?

00:09:15.630 --> 00:09:18.440
Wait, I'm a high school girl!

00:09:18.440 --> 00:09:20.010
Not just similar.

00:09:20.010 --> 00:09:23.090
When that old woman first 
arrived in this town...

00:09:23.090 --> 00:09:26.330
She wanted menko cards, too, just like you.

00:09:26.330 --> 00:09:30.190
How did she end up becoming 
an attendant at the bath?

00:09:33.510 --> 00:09:37.290
When did that happen?

00:09:38.160 --> 00:09:42.270
Like me, she wandered into town,

00:09:43.180 --> 00:09:46.020
and bought a bunch of masks and menko cards.

00:09:46.800 --> 00:09:52.730
Then she said she wanted to take a bath, 
so she was taken to the blended bath.

00:09:46.810 --> 00:09:53.780
<b>Blended Bath</b>

00:10:00.210 --> 00:10:03.260
The water's gotten worse recently.

00:10:03.260 --> 00:10:05.060
Your skin's starting to show its age.

00:10:05.060 --> 00:10:07.190
What about your flat chest?

00:10:07.190 --> 00:10:09.260
You should get that looked at soon.

00:10:09.260 --> 00:10:11.110
Maybe I'll visit a urologist.

00:10:11.110 --> 00:10:12.420
What are you talking about?

00:10:12.420 --> 00:10:15.360
The new urologist that opened up on 3-chome.

00:10:15.360 --> 00:10:18.300
Ah, the one with the macho 
and handsome director.

00:10:18.300 --> 00:10:20.560
Looking at him every day 
has anti-aging effects.

00:10:20.560 --> 00:10:21.760
Really?

00:10:21.760 --> 00:10:23.790
No, obviously not.

00:10:23.790 --> 00:10:26.120
Quick and efficient Takatsu Clinic.

00:10:26.120 --> 00:10:27.900
They don't accept insurance.

00:10:27.900 --> 00:10:28.820
And it hurts.

00:10:28.820 --> 00:10:29.710
And it's expensive.

00:10:29.710 --> 00:10:32.130
Speaking of expensive, 
there's that designer apartment complex.

00:10:32.130 --> 00:10:33.510
What are you talking about?

00:10:33.510 --> 00:10:36.840
That new rental property on 4-chome.

00:10:37.510 --> 00:10:40.140
You mean that pointlessly green 
building shaped like a toilet seat?

00:10:40.140 --> 00:10:42.890
Looking at it every day makes me feel 
like a socialite with a hot body.

00:10:42.890 --> 00:10:44.120
Really?

00:10:44.120 --> 00:10:46.030
No, obviously not.

00:10:46.030 --> 00:10:49.080
Nothing's better than a bath 
and a lymphatic massage.

00:10:49.080 --> 00:10:51.360
Quick and efficient hormone therapy.

00:10:51.360 --> 00:10:52.430
It doesn't hurt.

00:10:52.430 --> 00:10:53.410
And it's free.

00:10:58.420 --> 00:11:15.650
<b>Women's Bath</b>

00:10:58.420 --> 00:11:15.650
<b>Men's Bath</b>

00:10:58.980 --> 00:11:05.890
Until that old woman who looks like me 
sat in the attendant's seat at the bath,

00:11:06.440 --> 00:11:09.380
nobody sat in that seat.

00:11:09.900 --> 00:11:15.060
Apparently customers visiting the baths 
would sit in the attendant's seat.

00:11:15.840 --> 00:11:17.000
Truly.

00:11:17.000 --> 00:11:18.700
This is, without a doubt...

00:11:18.700 --> 00:11:20.190
Paradise.

00:11:20.490 --> 00:11:21.530
They're right.

00:11:21.530 --> 00:11:26.270
But why am I alone allowed to 
enjoy this meaningless paradise?

00:11:26.870 --> 00:11:29.220
It's probably your past life.

00:11:29.560 --> 00:11:31.550
What are you talking about?

00:11:31.550 --> 00:11:32.670
It's karma.

00:11:32.670 --> 00:11:34.370
Your fate from a past life.

00:11:34.370 --> 00:11:36.130
You guys...

00:11:36.130 --> 00:11:39.220
Do you guys actually...

00:11:39.220 --> 00:11:42.440
Do you guys actually believe in past lives?

00:11:43.000 --> 00:11:45.120
If we didn't have past lives...

00:11:45.120 --> 00:11:46.400
...then we...

00:11:46.780 --> 00:11:48.530
...wouldn't be alive.

00:11:48.870 --> 00:11:52.140
Why? Why wouldn't you be alive?

00:11:52.140 --> 00:11:54.170
Because if we didn't have past lives...

00:11:54.170 --> 00:11:55.830
...then we would be like...

00:11:56.400 --> 00:11:58.260
Like what?

00:11:59.210 --> 00:12:00.200
Bathwater.

00:12:00.360 --> 00:12:05.320
<b>Are you a ghost?!</b>

00:12:05.890 --> 00:12:10.830
So, what happened to the attendant 
who looks like me after that?

00:12:10.830 --> 00:12:12.170
Nothing, really.

00:12:12.170 --> 00:12:13.390
She actually still sits...

00:12:13.390 --> 00:12:16.010
In the attendant's seat at the bath.

00:12:16.010 --> 00:12:18.130
She really does look like you, though.

00:12:18.130 --> 00:12:19.380
Even your voices are the same.

00:12:19.380 --> 00:12:21.140
You probably have similar 
personalities, too.

00:12:21.140 --> 00:12:24.820
Then I'll just have to enter the bath, too.

00:12:24.820 --> 00:12:25.860
What did you say?

00:12:25.860 --> 00:12:27.130
You can't do that!

00:12:27.130 --> 00:12:30.400
If you do that, something 
terrible will happen!

00:12:30.400 --> 00:12:34.560
What do you mean, "terrible"?

00:12:36.810 --> 00:12:38.690
Get Katsuno!

00:12:38.690 --> 00:12:40.150
Someone get Katsuno!

00:12:40.150 --> 00:12:41.790
Get Katsuno!

00:12:41.790 --> 00:12:45.080
Don't bring that gorilla here!

00:12:45.080 --> 00:12:46.620
Didn't you need a doctor?

00:12:46.620 --> 00:12:47.650
A doctor!

00:12:47.650 --> 00:12:50.600
Weren't you looking for a doctor?

00:12:50.600 --> 00:12:52.470
That doesn't matter anymore!

00:12:52.470 --> 00:12:57.760
I'm going to sit in the attendant's 
seat for no reason at all!

00:12:57.760 --> 00:12:59.170
If you...

00:12:59.170 --> 00:13:00.710
If you sit there...

00:13:00.710 --> 00:13:04.200
If you sit in the attendant's seat 
for no reason at all, then...

00:13:41.780 --> 00:13:44.260
Why are you acting like that?!

00:13:52.140 --> 00:14:01.610
Makkiriya

00:13:56.200 --> 00:13:59.680
Miss, come have a drink.

00:14:06.810 --> 00:14:11.510
Despite being penniless, you were 
looking around for a doctor?

00:14:11.510 --> 00:14:13.620
How truly astonishing.

00:14:13.620 --> 00:14:19.650
It's true that I'm looking for a doctor, 
but I promise I'm not messing around.

00:14:20.030 --> 00:14:26.330
If anything, having a drink at this place 
and sulking in bed would be far easier.

00:14:27.000 --> 00:14:29.870
Mai, do you work as a hostess here?

00:14:29.870 --> 00:14:33.560
I was sold here from Transylvania.

00:14:34.250 --> 00:14:36.980
I'm the unhappiest girl in the world.

00:14:37.520 --> 00:14:40.550
So, tell me about your 
parents who sold you off.

00:14:41.410 --> 00:14:44.050
My father comes from an 
unaccomplished family.

00:14:44.050 --> 00:14:46.650
Is he that man taking a bath over there?

00:14:50.700 --> 00:14:54.870
My unaccomplished father won't listen to me.

00:14:54.870 --> 00:14:57.600
Is he really that unreasonable?

00:14:57.600 --> 00:14:59.000
He refuses to hear what I have to say.

00:14:59.000 --> 00:15:03.190
And what about the master of 
this house who bought you?

00:15:03.190 --> 00:15:07.190
The woman who bought me comes 
from an unaccomplished family.

00:15:08.760 --> 00:15:10.840
I have no idea what's going on.

00:15:10.840 --> 00:15:14.210
Sounds like a rather 
complicated relationship.

00:15:14.210 --> 00:15:15.780
Thank you for waiting.

00:15:24.280 --> 00:15:27.220
You seem quite accustomed to working here.

00:15:27.220 --> 00:15:29.670
What kind of name is Mai?

00:15:29.670 --> 00:15:33.820
I told you, my name is 
Mai Vlad Transylvania.

00:15:33.820 --> 00:15:38.850
In that case, Mai Vlad Transylvania-san, 
would you like a drink?

00:15:38.850 --> 00:15:41.150
Hey, ma. Wanna drink?

00:15:41.710 --> 00:15:43.830
That's an obscure reference.

00:15:44.160 --> 00:15:47.220
What I desire starts with the letter B.

00:15:47.220 --> 00:15:49.160
Is that a riddle?

00:15:49.160 --> 00:15:52.560
Starts with the letter B? Is it biscuit?

00:15:52.560 --> 00:15:54.890
I'm tired of eating biscuits.

00:15:54.890 --> 00:15:57.550
B*ner? No, it couldn't be that.

00:15:57.550 --> 00:16:00.350
I can't believe I said that!

00:16:00.690 --> 00:16:04.960
This drink seems to turn 
me into an indecent drunk.

00:16:04.960 --> 00:16:07.830
It's castor oil and water.

00:16:07.830 --> 00:16:12.540
I see. There's no underage 
drinking happening here.

00:16:12.530 --> 00:16:15.280
<b>Self-censored</b>

00:16:15.490 --> 00:16:18.170
What I desire is blood.

00:16:18.170 --> 00:16:22.200
Mai, is blood all you think about?

00:16:22.200 --> 00:16:26.320
For example, do you think 
nothing of your circumstances?

00:16:26.320 --> 00:16:27.790
They are miserable.

00:16:27.790 --> 00:16:31.880
You hardly seem miserable to me.

00:16:32.180 --> 00:16:33.960
I can't help that.

00:16:33.960 --> 00:16:38.050
Don't you have anything more nuanced to say?

00:16:38.050 --> 00:16:41.290
Are you drunk on castor oil?

00:16:41.290 --> 00:16:43.850
I shall take good care of you.

00:16:43.850 --> 00:16:47.410
That's all right. It seems my 
behavior was a bit abrupt.

00:16:47.910 --> 00:16:52.650
Rather, I get the feeling that I shouldn't 
be sitting around here drinking.

00:16:52.650 --> 00:16:55.510
Like I have something 
more important to do...

00:16:57.240 --> 00:17:04.210
<b>Blade Steak</b>

00:16:57.600 --> 00:16:59.640
So you finally remembered.

00:16:59.640 --> 00:17:01.290
Huh? Well, if it isn't Katsuno.

00:17:01.290 --> 00:17:03.140
Don't give me that crap!

00:17:03.140 --> 00:17:04.320
Am I wrong?

00:17:04.690 --> 00:17:06.460
He's Katsuno of Shinden.

00:17:06.460 --> 00:17:08.260
Katsuno of Shinden?

00:17:08.260 --> 00:17:10.860
What does Katsuno of Shinden do?

00:17:10.860 --> 00:17:13.400
He's a delinquent of the 
night school's class 2-B.

00:17:13.400 --> 00:17:15.650
A villainous and horrible man.

00:17:16.020 --> 00:17:18.520
Every day he comes to torment me.

00:17:19.030 --> 00:17:21.640
And when he doesn't, I'm made to stand here.

00:17:22.090 --> 00:17:25.400
You two have found some nerve 
recently, haven't you?

00:17:25.400 --> 00:17:26.380
I wouldn't know.

00:17:26.940 --> 00:17:31.660
Keep speaking to me like that, 
and I'll tell Doctor Chihiro about it.

00:17:31.980 --> 00:17:34.770
You're from Tokyo, aren't you?

00:17:34.770 --> 00:17:37.560
Probably, I think.

00:17:37.560 --> 00:17:39.180
Probably?

00:17:39.180 --> 00:17:42.540
Apparently, it's still unclear 
where this series is set.

00:17:42.540 --> 00:17:45.110
Mai-chan, how much do I owe you?

00:17:45.110 --> 00:17:47.990
A mere five yen.

00:17:47.990 --> 00:17:51.590
Really? After all I drank and ate?

00:17:51.590 --> 00:17:55.000
That's super cheap. Lucky me.

00:17:55.000 --> 00:17:57.430
That can't be possible!

00:18:03.880 --> 00:18:05.070
A flower.

00:18:05.970 --> 00:18:09.200
It's a flower. A red flower.

00:18:09.940 --> 00:19:30.100
Gyoza General

00:18:09.940 --> 00:19:30.100
OB-GYN

00:18:12.420 --> 00:18:17.350
So, what kind of doctor are you looking for?

00:18:17.800 --> 00:18:19.480
One who accepts insurance.

00:18:19.480 --> 00:18:22.910
If possible, it's definitely necessary 
that I find a female doctor.

00:18:22.910 --> 00:18:26.230
Then you should visit the 
doctor in my building.

00:18:26.230 --> 00:18:29.420
Ma'am, you made quite a bit 
of money for yourself.

00:18:30.360 --> 00:18:35.900
This building was constructed off of your 
patented pot sticker making technique, wasn't it?

00:18:35.900 --> 00:18:40.940
It was certainly innovative to mix garlic 
into the skins of the gyoza itself.

00:18:41.370 --> 00:18:48.310
However, my mother came up with the 
idea before she left our home.

00:18:48.310 --> 00:18:49.540
Uh, oh.

00:18:50.510 --> 00:18:55.830
Could it be that you're my mother?

00:18:55.830 --> 00:18:57.740
That's who you are, isn't it?

00:18:58.140 --> 00:19:01.250
You're my mother from before I was born.

00:19:01.820 --> 00:19:05.460
There's a reason for this.

00:19:06.490 --> 00:19:10.130
What reason? Tell me.

00:19:10.420 --> 00:19:16.900
To do that, I must explain how the skins 
of my special gyoza are made.

00:19:16.900 --> 00:19:22.880
But that would surely bore the audience.

00:19:23.210 --> 00:19:27.490
I see. In that case, I 
can't ask you about that.

00:19:35.560 --> 00:19:39.590
Doctor Chihiro, please 
perform surgery on me!

00:19:39.590 --> 00:19:44.780
Private or public, you don't belong here.

00:19:44.780 --> 00:19:47.910
I'm a insurance doctor who 
specializes in blood.

00:19:47.910 --> 00:19:51.430
Please! This is no time to 
argue about the details!

00:19:51.430 --> 00:19:54.590
I might die of blood loss.

00:19:55.040 --> 00:19:57.320
My precious blood...

00:19:57.760 --> 00:20:00.060
Mai's blood!

00:20:00.060 --> 00:20:04.000
Fine, then. Perhaps I'll 
play doctor with you.

00:20:04.000 --> 00:20:07.440
What? Are you sure?

00:20:07.440 --> 00:20:09.690
But I'm a girl.

00:20:09.690 --> 00:20:13.360
Fool! Of course not!

00:20:12.980 --> 00:20:18.940
<b>SLAP SLAP SLAP</b>

00:20:24.540 --> 00:20:29.780
Doctor, you must be out of your mind!

00:20:29.780 --> 00:20:34.600
Shut up! Hold still!

00:20:37.420 --> 00:21:00.400
<b>Self-censored</b>

00:20:40.340 --> 00:20:43.580
Looks like the surgery was successful.

00:20:43.580 --> 00:20:47.180
Listen closely. You mustn't 
tighten that bolt.

00:20:47.180 --> 00:20:50.350
It'll stop the flow of your blood.

00:20:50.350 --> 00:20:53.850
Doctor Chihiro, I didn't know 
you could perform surgery, too.

00:20:53.850 --> 00:20:56.590
I simply utilized the bolt style.

00:20:56.590 --> 00:20:59.390
The world has progressed quite a bit.

00:21:04.960 --> 00:21:13.880
<i>And so, we were able to prevent my precious 
blood from spilling pointlessly.</i>

00:21:15.060 --> 00:21:21.110
<i>All my blood exists to be given to Mai.</i>

00:21:22.130 --> 00:21:31.110
<i>As long as I have this bolt, every last 
drop of my blood belongs to Mai.</i>

00:21:32.220 --> 00:21:40.010
<i>However, tightening this bolt 
causes my left arm to go numb.</i>

00:21:40.870 --> 00:21:43.460
<i>But don't read into it too deeply.</i>

00:21:44.140 --> 00:21:52.330
<i>There's no deeper or secret meaning 
behind it being my left arm.</i>

00:21:52.910 --> 00:22:02.420
<b>RRRUMBLE</b>

00:22:02.420 --> 00:22:14.980
This work is an homage to Tsuge Yoshiharu.
The dialogue and setting were inspired by <i>Screw Style</i>,
<i>Master of the Gensenkan Inn</i>, <i>Red Flowers</i>, and <i>The Girl of Mokkiriya</i>.

00:23:44.980 --> 00:23:59.990
<b>Episode 10 "Fiancé's a Frankenstein's Monster"</b>

00:23:45.840 --> 00:23:49.890
I know it's sudden, but allow me 
to introduce our transfer student,

00:23:49.890 --> 00:23:52.290
Franken Yasohachi-kun.

00:23:52.290 --> 00:23:54.590
Play nice, everyone.

00:23:54.940 --> 00:23:58.280
Doctor, you unplugged this, right?!
